<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy — ScoutStreak"
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  updatedDate="April 20, 2026"
  canonical="https://scoutstreak.com/privacy"
>
  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    ScoutStreak LLC ("ScoutStreak," "we," "us," or "our") operates the website at
    scoutstreak.com and the ScoutStreak mobile application. This Privacy Policy explains
    how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you interact with
    our services.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you sign up for our launch list, we collect your email address and the role you
    select (athlete, parent, coach, recruiter, athletic director, or other). This information
    is stored via our API and used exclusively to send you product updates and launch
    notifications.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you use the ScoutStreak mobile application, we may collect additional information
    including your name, sport, position, school, graduation year, athletic statistics,
    highlight media, and recruiting activity. The mobile application has its own terms
    and privacy disclosures available within the app.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To communicate product updates, launch dates, and development milestones</li>
    <li>To improve our services based on aggregate usage patterns</li>
    <li>To respond to your inquiries and support requests</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information. We may share data with service providers
    who assist in operating our platform (such as email delivery and hosting services),
    but only to the extent necessary and under appropriate confidentiality agreements.
  </p>

  <h2>GDPR and CCPA Compliance</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a resident of the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, you have
    rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). If you are a California
    resident, you have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). These
    rights include the right to access, correct, delete, and port your personal data,
    and the right to opt out of certain processing activities.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
    <li>Object to or restrict certain processing</li>
    <li>Receive your data in a portable format</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller responsible for your personal information is ScoutStreak LLC,
    located in Hampshire, Illinois, United States.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the
    purposes described in this policy, or as required by law. Launch list email
    addresses are retained until you unsubscribe or request deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We implement appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect your
    personal information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or
    destruction.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions, data access requests, or to exercise any of your rights,
    contact us at
    <a href="mailto:swinnett@scoutstreak.com" class="text-gold hover:underline">swinnett@scoutstreak.com</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
